Subject: [PATCH] net: accept credentials in the --proxy-server URL

--proxy-server=socks5://user:pass@host:port works. The browser takes the
username and password off each proxy URI, percent-decodes them, and
hands Chromium the bare scheme://host:port. The credential is held in
the browser's memory and kept off its command line, which
chrome://version, net-export, DevTools and crash keys can all show.
Child processes receive it inside their --apostate-profile payload. Two
proxy URIs with different credentials refuse the launch, as do
credentials on direct:// or quic://.

