+// The credential this launch adopted off `--proxy-server`'s userinfo, held in
+// memory for the process lifetime and never on the command line.
+//
+// Declared here so Profile::proxy_credentials() can fall back to it at *read*
+// time rather than having it baked in when the Profile was parsed. That
+// distinction is load-bearing: Profile::Get() caches its answer in a
+// function-local static on first call, and the first call can precede the
+// startup hook that does the adoption. Baking it in at parse time meant a
+// launch whose profile happened to be parsed early authenticated with nothing
+// -- which is exactly what `--single-process` did, observed against a live
+// proxy. Reading it here cannot be raced by whoever calls Get() first.
+BASE_EXPORT const std::optional<ProxyCredentials>& AdoptedProxyCredentials();
+
